  "instructions": {
    "chars": 727,
    "tokens": 146,
    "tokensCl100k": 146,
    "approxTokens": 182,
    "text": "Manage and use stored SSH connections. Call list_connections to discover aliases before running commands. run_command is a one-shot non-interactive shell; state does not persist between calls. Set cwd or include cd in the command. Connections are pooled, so repeated calls reuse a warm SSH session; pass reuse=false to force a fresh one. Output is capped and reports truncation; use maxOutputBytes or tail for large logs. On failure read errorKind and hint before retrying; unknown host keys are trusted once by default (acceptNewHostKey=false disables that). Use run_on_many for fleet checks, copy_file for transfers, and write_remote_file for small config writes. Read the sshya://guide resource for conventions and examples."
  },
